    "title": "041: Agent Registry, Routing and Role Extensions: Scaling the Fleet Without Taxing the Orchestrator"
  },
  "summary": {
    "kind": "quote",
    "span": {
      "end": 2162,
      "end_line": 22,
      "line": 20,
      "start": 1535
    },
    "text": "Two operator goals, one mechanism:\n1. **Scale the fleet.** An organization may define hundreds of specialist agents in bundles. The orchestrator's context must not grow with them, and no agent may become undispatchable by silent truncation (§3, §4).\n2. **Extend a role.** A bundle teaches a built-in role its own craft (`builder` learns a company's C++ stack; the same role in an art collective learns sculpture practice): more **skills**, more **guidance**, and a **team** of specialists attached to the role (§5). Extensions travel in bundles, so they inherit Xenia's signing, provenance, trust, update and rollback (§8)."
  }
